  "verification": "Existing4GPUFourier/RHS controls passed3.69s after genericpoint-map interface;2 independent paired-source quadrature/chain-rule checks and2 local-image-bound checks passed0.86s. No duplicate backend or compatibility wrapper.",
  "review": "Independent source reviewer approved shifted-source signs, effectiveS/J equations, full auxiliary trace, mean trace retention, ownership and local Fourier derivative-bound mathematics. Floating allowance is not an interval proof; image admissibility does not certify wet cutting or HOS continuation.",
  "conclusions": [
    "Moving elevated imageplanes hardly changes rollload, yet both can share substantial Fourierlift error. Image-plane agreement alone is insufficient.",
    "At64m/129grid,elevatedplanes give rollA1209.53 vs zero-plane1094.54. Fine64m/1025 gives1095.72(~0.108%high), but the full normalmatrix defect remains~21% and fixed physical near-rim trace residual~5.2%of bodypotentialpeak. Do not qualify the operator from selected inertia diagonals.",
    "The local admissibility condition is2h-Pz>=eta_aux(Pxy) for every sourcepoint, INCLUDING the auxiliarygraph extensioninsidehull. A faraway crestdoesnot constrain an image at anotherXY. The initial globalmaximum requirement was self-imposed and unnecessarilystrong.",
    "A local-node maximum plus Fourierderivative bounds covers the sourceprojection; rounding allowance is explicit and not interval arithmetic. Flat localboundh~1.18e-10m recovers directzeroplanemaps/loads at coarse129grid through the SAMEformula, with~1.7e-6kg heave/~3.9e-7kgm2 roll difference and~3e-10relative offgridtrace.",
